# Rust build output
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
rustc-ice-*.txt

# wasm-pack output and the npm package's own trees. `dist/` is already ignored
# unanchored below; the js path is listed again so the rule reads where the
# artefact actually lands without hunting the Python block. wasm-pack's
# `--out-dir js/pkg` writes beside the package manifest, so the binding's
# bundle is excluded there as well as at wasm-pack's own default location, and
# `--out-dir js/pkg-node` is the same build for the CommonJS target.
crates/opportune-wasm/pkg/
crates/opportune-wasm/js/pkg/
crates/opportune-wasm/js/pkg-node/
crates/opportune-wasm/js/node_modules/
crates/opportune-wasm/js/dist/
# The runtime-integration harnesses under `integration/` are private to `make
# test-wasm-*` and to the CI jobs that run them: each carries its own committed
# lockfile, installs into its own `node_modules`, and writes temporary test state
# beside its config (`.wrangler/`, `.vitest/`). None of it is part of the published
# package, which ships only `crates/opportune-wasm/js/dist/`.
crates/opportune-wasm/integration/*/node_modules/
crates/opportune-wasm/integration/*/.wrangler/
crates/opportune-wasm/integration/*/.vitest/
# The doc-snippet gate's scratch tree: it compiles the extracted snippets inside the
# package so their imports resolve to it, and removes the tree when it finishes.
crates/opportune-wasm/js/.doc-snippets-*/
# The suite's scratch tree for the top-level `using` case: the module has to sit inside
# the package so `opportune` resolves through the package's own name, and the case
# removes the tree when it finishes.
crates/opportune-wasm/js/tests/.top-level-using-*/

# Python build output and caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.so
*.pyd
*.egg-info/
/build/
# Unanchored: `uv build --out-dir dist` writes relative to the working directory, so
# a build run from crates/opportune-py leaves its output there.
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# Local environment files — never commit credentials
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem

# Bun lockfiles: the npm package is managed through npm (package-lock.json is
# committed), so a stray `bun install` in crates/opportune-wasm/js must not add a
# second lockfile for a different resolver.
bun.lock
bun.lockb

# Editors and OS files
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local tooling state
.shipwright/
# Internal planning material (spec, execution plan): reference input only, never
# shipped. docs/ is reserved for the published documentation site.
reference/

# mkdocs build output
/site/
